  '<p class="gd-p">You keep the money right: payments, deposits and refunds, toll notices, processor payouts and Turo trips. There is no commission for Finance, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.</p><p class="gd-p">Your rail: Queue, Today, Money, Tolls and tickets, Turo trips, Find a renter, Calendar and Scorecard. <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> opens with a row of tabs on top, as in Admin: <b class="gd-ui">To handle</b> (payments, deposits, refunds), <b class="gd-ui">By day</b> (with Today, 7 days, 30 days and 90 days), <b class="gd-ui">All payments</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Refunds</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Deposits</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Reconciliation</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Unlinked Stripe</b> (the Stripe payments of the last 60 days that no booking knows, checked every night, with a best guess of the booking: an Admin links one from the booking&#39;s Money tab; put one aside with the reason when it is not a booking&#39;s payment). <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b> lists every owner invoice and owner statement. The old Payments by day and Reconciliation addresses open their tabs.</p><section class="gd-task" id="finance-your-queue" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your queue</h2><p class="gd-p">Finance tasks include failed owner debits, toll notices with no match, statements to review and refunds to issue.</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/940"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-01-queue-desktop-2f37513d.jpg" alt="The lanes show what Finance handles: payments to fix, refunds waiting, tolls and tickets, deposits to settle and owner statements. Money today counts them below." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="940"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.3%;top:24.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div><figcaption>The lanes show what Finance handles: payments to fix, refunds waiting, tolls and tickets, deposits to settle and owner statements. Money today counts them below.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-payments-by-day" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments by day</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">By day</b> tab, is your day in one screen: every payment and refund, by method, with the cash drawer and the refunds to decide.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose From and To (today by default) and tick the methods you want (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer and others; none ticked shows all), then press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Totals by method: received, refunded and net. Each day: the same by method, the cash expected in the drawer (cash received less cash given back) and the cash counted.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">At the end of the day count the drawer and press <b class="gd-ui">Record the count</b>. The difference shows &quot;balanced&quot;, or &quot;over&quot; or &quot;short&quot; with the amount.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere (a cancellation, a booking, Finance), with the policy maths (paid, the tier, the percentage back, what is kept). Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with the reason in the same row; above your limit it says an Admin approves. Approved: <b class="gd-ui">Issue the refund</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Export CSV</b> gives the same rows for the bank or the bookkeeper: refunds as negative amounts, holds marked as not money in.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-payments-deposits-refunds" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments, deposits, refunds</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">To handle</b> tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Failed payments: each with the purpose, amount and the bank&#39;s reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Deposits to take before pickup, and deposits due back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Refunds in progress. Press <b class="gd-ui">Request the refund</b> and choose What it refunds (the rental charge, delivery or pickup, kilometres, add-ons or other charges); above your limit it waits for an Admin. Then <b class="gd-ui">Issue the refund</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owner invoices that failed, and owner statements to prepare.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/money</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/865"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-02-money-desktop-486a8fbc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="865"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.6%;top:60.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.4%;top:21.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:73.2%;top:33.8%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:11%;top:45.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-a-payment-received-another-way" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A payment received another way</h2><p class="gd-p">An owner or renter paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Owner invoice: on <b class="gd-ui">Payments, deposits, refunds</b>, find it under Owner invoices owing and press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Renter: beside the failed payment, press <b class="gd-ui">Paid another way</b>. Or open the booking&#39;s Money tab: in Rental charges press Collect (the amount) rental, or in Security deposit Collect (the amount) deposit, choose <b class="gd-ui">Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)</b> and how it was paid, then record it. Each panel collects its own part only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance; type less for a partial payment.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the proof if you have it (a screenshot or a photo of the cheque), then press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The invoice is marked paid or partly paid, the automatic debit stops for that amount and the owner gets a receipt. Above your single limit the payment needs an Admin. Recorded something wrong? Ask an Admin to void it; you cannot void a payment.</p><p class="gd-p">Each month&#39;s payments recorded by hand are listed under Reconciliation, with the totals by method, to check against the bank.</p><p class="gd-p">A pay link for the rental, the fees or the balance asks for what is owed and never more (release 48): the booking&#39;s total less every payment of it, refunds counted back. After a change to the total, the link is for the difference. A booking paid in full gets no balance link: anything on top is a later charge, with its reason. A new link replaces any open one for the booking&#39;s money, and a link still open when a payment lands is cancelled by itself (the booking history says so), so the renter is never charged twice.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-cards-holds-and-deposits-given-back" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cards, holds and deposits given back</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking&#39;s Money tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">After the return, <b class="gd-ui">Charge the renter</b>: the Reason from the list (Other with its note), the Amount, and the line that says where the money comes from (the deposit hold while it is valid, else the card on file, else a pay link) before you press <b class="gd-ui">Charge $...</b>. Before the return, Rental charges, <b class="gd-ui">A later charge</b>, with the same reason list on the renter&#39;s receipt. A deposit that cannot be held: Security deposit, <b class="gd-ui">Charge the card on file as the deposit</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A deposit hold, in the Security deposit panel: <b class="gd-ui">Keep part (damage/fees)</b> with the amount and the reason from the list (the rest is released), or <b class="gd-ui">Release</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Hold expired</b>: nothing can be kept from it; press <b class="gd-ui">Charge the card on file instead</b> (the amount and the reason are filled in). While the car is out, inside the toll window or while something is open, both wait for the settlement; an Admin may do it with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way: the task Give the deposit back the way it came; then press <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b> with the reference or receipt number.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-settle-a-deposit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Settle a deposit</h2><p class="gd-p">The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking&#39;s Money tab, under Deposit, press <b class="gd-ui">Settle the deposit</b>. Issue the Check-out statement first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Damage: an Admin keeps the whole deposit (<b class="gd-ui">Keep the whole deposit (damage)</b>) or bills a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible. Ask an Admin, with the photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Settle</b>. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A card hold lapses after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-read-a-toll-notice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Read a toll notice</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Tolls and tickets</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Read a notice</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the file: a PDF, a photo or a CSV, under 15 MB. Leave the reading profile to find it from the text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Read it</b>. Then check each line beside the notice and fix what was read wrong.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Checked against the notice</b> on each line (<b class="gd-ui">Leave out</b> to skip one), then <b class="gd-ui">Save as checked</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Confirm and import</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/tolls/read</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/580"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-04-tolls-read-desktop-aa04a6b2.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="580"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.5%;top:44.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.1%;top:64.8%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.1%;top:89.7%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>In the work queue, <b class="gd-ui">Match again</b> retries the match after a fix, and <b class="gd-ui">Dispute</b> marks a notice you think is wrong. Renters matched with high confidence are charged at import, with the notice and our fee.</div></aside><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/tolls</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/540"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-03-tolls-desktop-37b6f99c.jpg" alt="The work queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged and Disputed, with each notice&#39;s plate, date, amount and match." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="540"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:23.6%;top:12.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div><figcaption>The work queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged and Disputed, with each notice&#39;s plate, date, amount and match.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-reconciliation-and-turo-trips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Reconciliation and Turo trips</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Reconciliation</b> tab: press <b class="gd-ui">Record a processor payout</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Match</b> it to the payments it contains. Anything still unmatched at the closing check goes to an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turo trips</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Add a trip</b> for one trip, or paste CSV rows and press <b class="gd-ui">Import</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/turo</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/540"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-06-turo-desktop-b59cc7f9.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="540"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95.1%;top:14.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-deposits-to-release" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposits to release</h2><p class="gd-p">A deposit is never released by itself. Each morning the system puts one task in your queue for every deposit due back: &quot;Release the deposit for&quot; the booking, with the amount and the day it is due (7 business days after the check-out, or after the return when no check-out was recorded). On the day, and every day after, you and the Admins also get a notice in the portal. Nothing is emailed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the task: it opens the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Settle the deposit: apply what is owed, hold back what an open item needs, release the rest.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The task closes by itself once nothing is left to give back.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Card payments outside the site and the card reader</h3><p class="gd-p">On a booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab: <b class="gd-ui">Record card payment</b> records a card taken in the Stripe Dashboard or on a reader (the last 4 digits always; a Stripe payment id, pi_..., checks it, and a deposit hold needs it). <b class="gd-ui">Charge on reader</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Hold deposit on reader</b> send the amount to the S700; the renter taps the card and the screen updates by itself. On a credit card coverage rental the whole rental is paid on the same card: another card is refused with the reason, and only an Admin can allow another one.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-deposit-holds-and-partner-invoices-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposit holds and partner invoices (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">Deposits stay as holds with Stripe and are never captured by itself. A job re-authorizes a hold by itself about 24 hours before it expires; when it cannot, you get the alert <b class="gd-ui">Deposit hold not re-authorized</b>. A <b class="gd-ui">The deposit hold expires soon</b> To do opens the booking: <b class="gd-ui">Re-authorize the hold</b> places a new hold on the saved card and releases the old one; or <b class="gd-ui">Keep part (damage/fees)</b> for only what is owed. A deposit not taken yet: in the Security deposit panel, <b class="gd-ui">Hold on the card on file</b>. Under <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partner invoices</b> you write invoices to body shops, tow trucks and storage yards for their kickback, send them, record the cheques and e-Transfers that come in, and export the CSV for the bookkeeper.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-kickbacks-and-repairs" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Kickbacks and repairs</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Kickbacks and repairs</b>: the kickbacks received on partner invoices (before HST) and the repair costs paid by CarmaCars for a period, by owner and by car, with the CSV. An invoice with no car counts nowhere until you choose it: open the invoice under <b class="gd-ui">Partner invoices</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Choose the car</b>. Add a repair cost with <b class="gd-ui">Add a repair cost</b>; Fleet adds them on the car&#39;s page too.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">A debit deposit&#39;s card fee</h3><p class="gd-p">A deposit charged (not held) on a debit or prepaid card carries the non-refundable <b class="gd-ui">Card processing fee for a debit deposit</b>, shown on its line in the history and on the receipt. The deposit refund returns the deposit only.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-partners-the-timesheet-and-ended-trips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Partners, the timesheet and ended trips</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">More finance</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b>: the rental partners (their pages, cars, rates, invoices) and the referral partners (kickbacks, payments), with every action an Admin has there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Timesheet</b>: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked. Add forgotten hours or void a wrong entry, with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Close ended trips</b>: mark trips that ended and were never closed, and choose the deposit decision. An Admin presses Release; nothing is released by itself.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-deposit-review-double-check-tolls-and-tickets-then-bill-or-r" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposit review: double-check, tolls and tickets, then bill or release</h2><p class="gd-p">Once Fleet signed every item of a returned booking you get a To do to double-check the deposit review. The deposit stays held until you signed every item too; only an Admin can release it earlier, with the reason.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Deposit reviews</b> and open the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Double-check</b> on each item: read Fleet&#39;s finding and the photos, then <b class="gd-ui">OK</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Issue</b> with the amount to bill. Someone else double-checks an item you signed for Fleet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Highway tolls</b>: open the toll operator&#39;s site from the review, search the plate for the rental dates, then double-check the item.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Tickets</b>: open each place in the list (its official lookup link), search the plate, and press <b class="gd-ui">None found</b> or <b class="gd-ui">A ticket</b>. A ticket is logged in <b class="gd-ui">Tolls and tickets</b> with the place and the plate and matched to the booking there. The Tickets item waits until every place is checked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Then open <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> on the booking: bill what is owed with the charge after the return, or release the deposit.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">The sweep, Monday, Wednesday and Friday</h3><p class="gd-p">On each sweep day a To do <b class="gd-ui">Deposit check sweep</b> lists every plate returned since the last sweep and every booking still inside the toll and ticket window. <b class="gd-ui">Deposit reviews</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">This sweep</b> shows them by plate with every link, so you check them in one go. The days are in Program settings.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Countdowns</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Countdowns</b> (and the top of <b class="gd-ui">To handle</b>, and each booking) shows the time left before each deposit hold expires (with when the automatic re-authorization runs, 24 hours before), before each deposit is due back to the renter, and before the next payment of a weekly, biweekly or monthly plan. Red is within 24 hours or late, amber within 48. Sort by any column. You get an alert at 48 and 24 hours, and the counts are in your morning digest.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Do sales too</h3><p class="gd-p">Under <b class="gd-ui">My numbers</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Do sales too</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">I want to do sales too</b>: the Sales path is added to your academy (your Finance work is never held by it), and the Sales pages open once you pass it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-the-fuel-line-on-the-deposit-review-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fuel line on the deposit review (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">The fuel item shows <b class="gd-ui">Suggested</b> with its working: the tank x the fuel missing x the pump price x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee. It is a line on the return charges, never charged by itself: sign the item, then bill it with the rest from the booking&#39;s Money. A pump receipt still wins: enter it when the car was filled up.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-statements-and-payroll-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Statements and payroll (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Statements cover the 8th to the 7th, paid on the 10th; amounts not yet collected from the renter are listed apart and paid on the statement after they come in.</li><li>Payroll every two weeks: prepare the run with any bonus or deduction and its reason, then send it for approval. An Admin approves and records the payments.</li><li>Field spending (release 50): each expense says whose money paid. You get an alert for each one. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with the reason (the person sees it). Own money is then owed to the person: <b class="gd-ui">Reimbursements owed</b> on Payroll and Field spending lists it per person; press <b class="gd-ui">Mark paid back</b> once it is paid with their pay.</li><li>Email: Settings, Usage shows the real daily capacity of our sending services together; nothing to count by hand.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-a-late-return-is-a-choice-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return is a choice (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Late return</b> with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge as an extension</b>: every started day late at the booking&#39;s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge extra days</b>: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the late return fee</b>: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge a custom amount</b>: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive it</b>: no charge, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the late return charge</b>. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.</p><p class="gd-p">Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do &quot;Late return: choose the charge&quot;. Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do &quot;Late return: approve the charge&quot; and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve as asked</b>, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-payments-by-e-transfer-or-cash-deposits-and-tips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments by e-Transfer or cash, deposits and tips</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b>: a payment of the whole total pays every line of the booking (the rental, short notice, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan), whichever part you record it for. When nothing is open, a booking waiting for payment is confirmed by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The deposit by e-Transfer or cash is doubled</b>: twice the car&#39;s deposit by default (Program settings). The Security deposit card shows both amounts (&quot;Credit card hold $300.00; e-Transfer or cash $600.00 (2x)&quot;), and the renter sees them on the offer and the pay page before paying.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Collect the deposit</b> &gt; Cash or e-Transfer: leave the amount empty to take what is owed. Less is recorded as a part (the card says <b class="gd-ui">under, still owed $X</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Collect the $X still owed</b> takes the rest); more is held and given back with the deposit (<b class="gd-ui">over, to return $X</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Change the deposit</b> on Edit booking (an Admin, with the reason), even while the booking waits for payment: the Money tab, the deposit link and Collect $X deposit follow at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Voided a deposit by mistake?</b> After the void the deposit is <b class="gd-ui">Not collected</b> again everywhere (the header too): record it again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Tips</b>: the renter can add one when paying, on the receipt and from the after-trip email. A tip in cash or by e-Transfer: <b class="gd-ui">Tips</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Record a tip</b>. Half goes to the booking&#39;s salesperson and half to the staff member at the handover; with no staff salesperson (a direct booking) CarmaCars keeps that half; one person who did both gets it all. An Admin can give one tip another split (<b class="gd-ui">All to ...</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Back to the usual split</b>). A tip is never part of the rental or the owner&#39;s share.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">A greyed-out button says under it what to do first.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-evidence-for-every-fee-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Evidence for every fee (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A fee waiting for its evidence stays off the statement; the rest goes as usual. Issuing a statement with only such a fee says what is missing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A To do in the Finance queue asks for a toll or ticket notice, a receipt or an invoice. Attach it on the Money tab (<b class="gd-ui">Attach evidence</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the evidence of a held fee arrives after the Check-out statement, you get <b class="gd-ui">Evidence attached: bill the fee that was waiting</b>: bill it from the Money tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Only an Admin charges a fee without its evidence, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-finance-dashboard-and-the-bank-release-49" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Finance dashboard and the bank (release 49)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Finance</b> is the money of the business on one page, read only: each figure opens the page where it is worked.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cash position</b>: the bank balance from the latest RBC import, Stripe&#39;s balance (available and pending) and its payouts on the way, and <b class="gd-ui">Free cash</b>: all of that less the deposits held as cash, the owner payouts due, the refunds owed and the HST owed. An account whose balance is more than a week old is marked: import this week&#39;s download.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money in</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Money out</b> for the month (Earlier month, Later month): rentals and charges taken, owner fees, insurers, tips (for the staff, never revenue); owner payouts due and paid on the 10th, commissions, expenses with HST and refunds.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Held for others</b>: deposits held as cash (owed back unless applied), deposit holds on cards (not money in the bank), what is kept back for claims and tolls, and refunds owed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">HST</b> for the quarter: collected (renters, owners, insurers) less paid (expenses, payouts to registered owners) is what is owed. An Insurance Fee never carries HST: a line that does is listed in red to correct.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Renter balances overdue</b> (past the statement&#39;s 7 days) and <b class="gd-ui">Insurer invoices unpaid</b> by age (0 to 30, 31 to 60, 61 to 90, over 90 days).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Twelve months</b>: money in, money out and net by month, beside the monthly statement&#39;s net where one is built.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bank lines</b> is the reconciliation:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">In RBC online banking open the account, <b class="gd-ui">Download transactions</b>, CSV or OFX (OFX also has the balance), and drop the file on <b class="gd-ui">Import from RBC online banking</b>. The file stays on your computer; only its lines are saved, with the last four digits of the account. Importing the same days again adds nothing. With a CSV, type the balance shown in online banking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A line that fits exactly one record matches by itself: money in to a Stripe payout, an e-Transfer, bank transfer or cheque recorded on a booking or owner invoice, or an insurer invoice; money out to an owner payout, a commission or referral partner payout, an expense or a refund sent by transfer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">No match</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Match</b> shows the records that fit (amount, and a date within a few days), nearest first: pick one. Nothing fits: record the payment, payout or expense first, then match. <b class="gd-ui">Set aside</b> a bank fee or a transfer between CarmaCars accounts, saying what it is. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> takes a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A line with no match after two days is a To do for Finance and in the Finance morning email; matching it closes the To do. Every step is in the audit log.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-check-e-transfer-release-49" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check e-Transfer (release 49)</h2><p class="gd-p">Sales reports an e-Transfer a renter sent, with the screenshot; nothing is recorded until you check the bank. You get an alert and a To do, <b class="gd-ui">Check e-Transfer</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the To do: the booking opens on its <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab. The card shows the amount, what it covers, the sender, who reported it and <b class="gd-ui">Open the screenshot</b>, and says what <b class="gd-ui">Confirm received</b> will record (for both, the deposit part is the deposit still owed by e-Transfer and the rest is the rental and fees).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">In the bank: type the <b class="gd-ui">Bank reference (optional)</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Confirm received</b>. It is recorded as Record a payment does (method e-Transfer; your single limit applies) and a booking waiting for payment with nothing open is confirmed. The screenshot becomes the payment&#39;s proof.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not there: <b class="gd-ui">Not received</b>, say why, <b class="gd-ui">Send back to the rep</b>. Nothing is recorded; the rep is told.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">You never check an e-Transfer you reported yourself.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'my-jobs', 'chapter', 'start-here', 'The portal has four tabs at the bottom of the screen: **Today**, **My shifts**, **My pay** and **Training** (and **Sales** if you asked to do sales too). Today is where the work is.

## Your shift and the clock

1. At the top of **Today**: your shift, and **Clock in**. Press it when you start. The phone shares where you are at that moment only.
2. The bar shows how many of the day''s must-dos are done.
3. When you finish, press **Clock out**. Anything still open is listed: give a reason for each, then press **Clock out with these reasons**. Fleet is told, so someone can cover them.

## One list, in order

The list is built for you from the bookings and the cars:

1. **Your work**: every pickup and return of the day (deliveries and collections too) at its time, and onboarding prep Fleet gave you. Each car and time is one card.
2. **When you have time**: cars to clean (not checked clean for a week), cars needing service or not roadworthy, and cars that need listing photos.
3. Switch to **Tomorrow** to see what is planned so far.

## Missing check-in and check-out

On **Today**: past rentals you handled or were given that are missing their photos and readings, closed bookings and pickups recorded with the details later included.

1. Press **Add the photos and readings** on one.
2. Add the odometer, the fuel and the damage photos, then save. Fleet can give you more of them.

## A card

1. The time, what it is (Pickup, Return, Delivery to the renter), the car and its plate, the renter and the booking.
2. The steps of the card, ticked as they are done: the clean check, the add-ons in the car, the pickup photos and handover.
3. One big button: the next thing to do. **Start the pickup** or **Start the return** opens the job screen, where the clean check and the add-ons come first.
4. **More** has the place with **Open in maps**, the call to the renter, and helping the renter.

The card''s **Prepare: put each in the car, then tick** checklist lists every add-on to put in the car with its quantity. The office sees your ticks as you go.

> Watch out: The pickup cannot be finished until every add-on (a child seat, for example) is ticked as in the car. If the trip must go without it, ask an Admin to override on the job.

## Clean checks

Every car is checked clean before each pickup and after each return: choose **Clean** or **Needs cleaning**, take the photo and press **Save the clean check**. On a cleaning card in spare time, press **Check it clean** the same way.

## Cars needing service, and listing photos

1. On a service card, press **Give an update** (taken in, at the shop, waiting for parts, sorted) and **Send the update to Fleet**.
2. On a photo card, press **Take the listing photos**: the photo shoot opens with the angles the listing is missing.

## Onboarding prep

Fleet gives you the prep of a car joining the fleet on a day you hold a shift. Press **Open the prep**, then each item: upload what it needs (the safety certificate with its date) and press **Mark it done**. When every item is done, the owner''s onboarding checklist updates and Fleet is told.

## The Add button

The red **Add** button at the bottom right of Today:

1. **Money spent**: gas, a wash, parts, parking. The amount, the car, the booking and a photo of the receipt, then **Send to Finance**. Finance approves it and pays you back if you used your own money. No receipt yet: you get a To do until you add it.
2. **Service record**: what was done, where, the odometer, the cost and the invoice photo, then **Record the service**. The car''s maintenance resets, the expense is made on the car, and Fleet and Finance are told.
3. **Photos of a car**: a photo and a note, saved on the car.
4. **A problem with a car**: damage, a warning light, a ticket or lost property (see Report, rentals, referrals and profile).

## Help a renter on the spot

From a card''s **More**, or with **Find the booking** on Help a renter (by booking number, name or phone):

1. **Take a payment** or **Take the deposit hold**: **Show a QR for their phone** (they pay on their own phone), **Text the link**, **Email the link**, or **Use the card reader** when you have it. Never type a card number.
2. The licence: check it in person on the pickup.
3. The agreement: **They sign on my phone**, with their own finger.

> Good to know: Refunds stay with Finance and Admin.

## Check the renter''s licence

The renter''s licence photos and selfie are checked before the handover. You can check them yourself, for a booking on one of your own jobs today or in the next 7 days. Everything you do is recorded with your name and "field staff".

1. My jobs shows **Licences to check** when the licence front, back or selfie of a renter on one of your jobs waits for a decision. The same check is on the job itself, under **Check the licence**.
2. Press **Review the licence**. The images open with the name, date of birth and licence details on the booking.
3. Look at each image and the licence reader''s lines under each driver (Pass or Flag: valid to the return, class, age, name and date of birth, the Ontario number, front and back): no sign of alteration, and the selfie matches the licence photo. A photo you take that is blurry or cut off says so at once: take it again.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**. The renter is told why and sends a new one.
5. Then press **Approve all**: everything still waiting is approved at once.
6. To look again at an image already approved or rejected, press **View** beside it (it opens for one minute and the view is logged). After the 90-day removal it reads **Removed on** and the date.

> Tip: The renter''s proof of coverage stays with the office. Meeting the renter at the handover? You can still check the original licence in person from the ready check (see A handover).

## Documents to sign

Your staff agreement, when CarmaCars sends it.

1. My jobs shows "You have a document to sign". Press **Read and sign**.
2. Check the key values at the top (your role, wage and start date), then press **Read the PDF** and read it.
3. Sign in a few steps: press **Send the code** and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
4. Press **Sign**. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.

## Move a car

1. Under Moving a car, press **Start a move**. Choose the Car and Why (for example Reposition).
2. Fill in From and the Odometer (km), then press **Start the move now**.
3. When you arrive, press **End the move**, fill in Now at and the odometer, then press **End the move now**.

## Call and text the renter

**Call** on a card opens the Quo app with the renter''s number, so the call comes from the CarmaCars number; **Text** opens a small window that sends from the CarmaCars number and keeps the text with the booking.

**Cars now** and **Map of your cars** are links at the bottom of Today.

## Start a handover in one tap (release 42)

On a pickup or a return that is not started yet, the job shows **Start the check-in now** (or **Start the check-out now**): one tap acknowledges the job, starts it and opens the one-screen handover. Not with the car yet? Press **Acknowledge** so the office knows you have the job, and start it later.

## Your location on a job

Accept the electronic monitoring policy once (you get a copy by email). While you are on shift or on a job, the CarmaCars app shares where you are so Fleet can dispatch and you can prove a pickup or return. During an active job it stays on; off duty nothing is taken. Turn it off between jobs in **Profile** > **Location on the live map**.', 'Today', 'Your shift, then one list of the day: each car and time is one card. The Add button, and helping a renter on the spot.',
